The requirement is to modify the existing program 'OA HR Add Public Holiday to Off In Lieu Bank Balance' to include TRANSOM Catering (Catering Payroll), using the new lookups 'XXOA_OFFIN_LIEU_EMP_TYPE_CAT' and 'XXOA_OFFIN_LIEU_EMP_GRADES_CAT', so that a Public Holiday is added to the 'Off In Lieu Bank Balance' only for Shift employees of Catering Payroll, irrespective of whether the lookup 'XXOA_OFFIN_LIEU_EMP_TYPE_CAT' is configured to include both Shift and Regular Employees, or only Shift Employees. 1 Considering the Shift Employee SN#20237 (Mr. Baburaj Kadamon Narayana Pillai), belonging to Catering Payroll. Note the Off In Lieu Bank Balance before testing. Scenario 1: With the lookup 'XXOA_OFFIN_LIEU_EMP_TYPE_CAT' configured to include both Shift and Regular Employees, run the program 'OA HR Add Public Holiday to Off In Lieu Bank Balance' with Payroll as 'Catering Payroll' for Test Holiday 1 and click Submit. Scenario 2: Reconfigure the lookup to include only Shift Employees, run the same program for Test Holiday 2 and click Submit. Verify the Off In Lieu Bank Balance after both scenarios. TC-01 Since SN#20237 is a Shift employee, the Public Holiday should be added to the Off In Lieu Bank Balance for both Test Holiday 1 (Scenario 1) and Test Holiday 2 (Scenario 2), irrespective of the lookup configuration. The Off In Lieu Bank Balance should increase by 1 day for each Test Holiday processed (a total increase of 2 days). PASS The Off In Lieu Bank Adjustment entry was created successfully for both Test Holiday 1 and Test Holiday 2, and the Off In Lieu Bank Balance for SN#20237 increased by 2 days in total, in both Scenario 1 and Scenario 2, as expected. Sai Vighnessh B L 06-Aug-26
